# Project Rules: The Eye Agent

## Stack
- Node.js (v24+) + TypeScript
- Telegram Bot Framework: Telegraf
- Database: SQLite (via better-sqlite3)
- i18n: 5 languages (fa, en, ar, tr, ru)
- AI: Gemini API Integration

## Guidelines
- Write modular, clean, and strongly typed TypeScript code.
- Prioritize security: Captcha first, then Rate Limiting, then AI processing.
- Keep handlers isolated in `src/bot/handlers/`.
- Maintain strict zero-budget policy using free/local tools.

## Folder Structure
- src/bot/handlers/ - Command handlers
- src/database/ - Database client and repositories
- src/locales/ - Language JSON files
- src/services/ - External services (Gemini, Telegram)
- src/middlewares/ - Auth, rate limiting, i18n
- src/config/ - Configuration and constants
- src/types/ - TypeScript type definitions
- src/utils/ - Helper functions

## Security Rules
- Captcha required before any Gemini API call
- Rate limiting: 5 messages per minute per user
- Captcha expiry: 60 seconds
- Max 3 failed captcha attempts → 24h ban